# --- "How to use" pages ---
unboundtech.research_page.TEMPERED_THAUMIUM.3=How to use this.<BR><BR>The furnace road: build an IC2 industrial blast furnace, give it compressed air and power, and put a thaumium ingot inside. Five minutes later you take out a tempered one.<BR><BR>The crucible road: heat a crucible, drop in an IC2 steel ingot and pour in four Praecantatio, two Permutatio and two Vitreus. The ingot surfaces on its own.<BR><BR>From there the metal goes anywhere a recipe asks for tempered thaumium: armour, tools, and the casings of the Phial Station, the Burner and both converters. It also repairs them, armour and tools alike, on an anvil.<BR><BR>The thaumium wrench (recipe on the last page) is made from ORDINARY thaumium, not tempered. Right-click a machine to rotate it, sneak and right-click to remove it with its buffer intact. It works on IC2 machines too.

unboundtech.research_page.TEMPERED_ARMOR.2=How to use this.<BR><BR>Forged at an ordinary bench in the familiar layouts: five ingots for the helmet, eight for the chestplate, seven for the leggings, four for the boots. Twenty-four for the full set.<BR><BR>Worn like any armour. Repaired on an anvil with a tempered thaumium ingot - two damaged pieces will also combine in the grid, but they lose their enchantments.<BR><BR>Remember the price: in a full set every wand casting costs a fifth more. If you do not cast at all there is no price for you, beyond the thin lists at the enchanting table.

unboundtech.research_page.TEMPERED_TOOLS.3=How to use this.<BR><BR>Ordinary bench, vanilla layouts: pickaxe and axe take three ingots and two sticks, the sword two and one, the shovel one and two, the hoe two and two.<BR><BR>The pickaxe handles obsidian and everything a diamond one does. Repaired on an anvil with a tempered thaumium ingot.<BR><BR>Enchant through infusion rather than the table: the table will offer short lists. The tools have no special effects - for those, go to the order's own tools.

unboundtech.research_page.ELECTRIC_SCRIBING.2=How to use this.<BR><BR>Just keep it in your inventory: the research table finds the first inkwell it sees and spends that one. If you carry both an ordinary inkwell and this, the table takes whichever sits earlier - put the other in a chest.<BR><BR>Recharge in any IC2 charger: a batbox, an MFE, an MFSU. The bar under the item shows the remaining charge, the tooltip shows how many notes are left.<BR><BR>A flat inkwell does not break or vanish: the table simply stops noticing it until you put it back on charge.


